    "content": "All 19 checklist items have been tested and recorded.\n\n## Summary\n\n**13 PASS / 6 FAIL**\n\nThe core happy paths work well: job posting, browsing, filtering, keyword search, job details, application submission, the employer dashboard with per-job application lists, and confirmed deletion all behave correctly.\n\n**Failures found:**\n\n| ID | Issue |\n|---|---|\n| **CS-10** | No job-posting validation at all — a job with min salary $200k > max $100k and zero skills was published successfully; empty form submit gives no feedback |\n| **CS-9** | Invalid applications are blocked *silently* — no toast, no inline error, no `aria-invalid`; the user never learns which field is wrong |\n| **CS-11** | Duplicate applications to the same job with the same email are accepted; no de-duplication |\n| **IX-19** | No persistence whatsoever — published jobs, submitted applications, and deletions all revert to seed data on reload (`localStorage`/`sessionStorage` empty) |\n| **FT-18** | Job editing is not implemented — no edit button anywhere, and `/employer/edit-job/:id` returns 404 |\n| **CT-20** | Off-by-one date bug — items created seconds ago render as \"Yesterday\" instead of today |\n\nThe two most impactful themes are **missing validation with silent failure** (CS-9, CS-10, CS-11) and **no data persistence** (IX-19), which together undermine the reliability of an otherwise functional application."
  }
}
